VL53L7CH/VL53L8CH
#################

Origin:
   ST Microelectronics
   https://www.st.com/en/embedded-software/stsw-img043.html

Status:
   version 2.0.16

Purpose:
   ST Microelectronics official Ultra Lite Driver (ULD) API to use vl53l7ch and vl53l8ch sensors.

Description:
   This library written by STMicroelectronics is dedicated to vl53l7ch/vl53l8ch time of flight sensors.
   Instead of providing a full description of the registers, ST decided to provide a C library to drive this sensor.

   The vl53l7ch and vl53l8ch share the same generic VL53LMZ API, so this single
   HAL serves both sensors (module type reported at runtime via
   VL53LMZ_MODULE_TYPE_L7 / VL53LMZ_MODULE_TYPE_L8).

   This library is called from the vl53lmz driver and is kept transparent for users.
   User is calling a standard Zephyr driver and then, the driver makes some calls to this library.

   In order to fit with Zephyr rules and simplify version updates, we have done a minimum of modifications :
      - split headers and source to inc/src
      - keep only the API directory
        (remove documentation and samples, see ST website for this)
      - drop the ST-provided platform stub; the Zephyr driver supplies its own

   In order to use this library, you have to :
      * define CONFIG_HAS_STLIB and CONFIG_VL53LMZ
      * include vl53lmz_api.h (plus the vl53lmz_plugin_*.h headers for the
        optional CNH / detection-thresholds / motion-indicator / xtalk
        plugins) in the driver; vl53lmz_platform.h is provided by the driver
        directory

Dependencies:
   This package depends on Zephyr I2C implementation and is linked statically.
   This library will be used by a standard Zephyr driver.

